# Compile-time oracle fixtures (packages/ui, type-contracts.oracle.test.ts).
# Written INSIDE the package and removed in afterAll — which does not run when the task is
# KILLED, and turbo kills sibling tasks the moment another package's suite fails. The residue
# then makes `pnpm verify` red on generated fixtures, pointing at the wrong defect entirely.
# Same class as the `out/` entry above (9ca0189: "verify was linting generated bundles").
# Agent worktrees (24 §3 step 8 isolation). Each parallel agent gets its own git worktree here so
# it cannot capture a sibling's half-written files — the failure that put a protected-path change
# into 8c03e4d under a message describing none of it. They are working copies of tracked content,
# never content in their own right, and must never be committed into the tree they were cut from.
.claude/worktrees/
.oracle-typecheck/
# Same pattern, same hazard: layout-physical.oracle.test.ts writes fixtures to
# packages/ui/.oracle-layout and removes them in afterAll — so a KILLED run leaves
# them in the tree, where they red `pnpm verify` on generated files. Ignored for
# the same reason its sibling above is.
.oracle-layout/

# apps/manager — `pnpm -C apps/manager bundle:check` output (Metro resolution proof, 05-F29)
.expo-bundle-check/
.expo/
